.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_BEGIN 3 2026-09-25 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_begin \- begin a filesystem MPQ update transaction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_begin(mpq_update_s **" "update" ", const char *" "path" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a same-directory private working copy of an existing regular MPQ or
container with an embedded MPQ at \fIpath\fP. The original file is unchanged
until commit. Embedded container prefixes and unrelated trailing bytes are
preserved; stale weak and strong signatures are removed on modification. On
failure, \fI*update\fP is NULL. MPQE archives require
\fBlibmpq__update_begin_mpqe\fP(3). The handle is consumed by commit or abort.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
V3/v4 mutations require complete filenames from the listfile, supplied member
names, or earlier successful operations. Unknown retained files, unresolved
aliases, BET-only classic attributes, embedded v3/v4 wrappers and patch members
are rejected without modifying the staged archive. Supported v3/v4 rebuilds
retain their version and regenerate mixed HET/BET and classic tables. Invalidated
signatures are removed. Unchanged commits and aborts require no reconstruction.
V4 preserves the source raw-chunk size, including zero, and regenerates
structural and member MD5 digests. Raw-enabled members are re-encoded at final
offsets; lossy recompression and unrepresentable sector-codec policies are rejected.
Repeated names differing only by ASCII case or slash direction are accepted.
Ambiguous names, embedded null bytes, unresolvable listfile entries and incomplete
filename coverage reject reconstruction. A staged close failure prevents further
mutation or publication; abort remains safe and attempts cleanup.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP on success, or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid paths, unsupported formats, allocation, and backing I/O errors are
returned as negative LIBMPQ_ERROR_* values.
